# Shader Pipeline Migration — Validation Rules

## Single validation command

Run the unified validator after every shader-related change:

```
dart tools/shader_port/bin/validate_migration.dart .
```

This executes all three pipeline stages in sequence and exits on the first failure.

### Flags

| Flag | Description |
|---|---|
| `[root]` | Project root directory (default: `.`) |
| `--skip-generate` | Skip Stage 1 (re-use already-generated `.metal` files) |
| `--verbose` / `-v` | Print the full command for each stage and all compile errors |
| `--strict` | Treat pair-validator warnings as errors |
| `--metal-std <version>` | Override Metal standard (default: `metal3.0`) |
| `--overrides <path>` | Override the shader pair overrides JSON path |

## Pipeline stages (run in order)

```
Stage 1 — generate:       dart tools/shader_port/lib/metal_generator.dart .
Stage 2 — compile-check:  dart tools/shader_port/bin/compile_check.dart .
Stage 3 — validate-pairs: dart tools/shader_port/bin/validate_pairs.dart RenderDll/XRenderMetal/Generated/generated_manifest.json
```

Never skip stages manually. The manifest is only valid after the generator runs.

## compile_check is the compilation gate

- `compile_check.dart` compiles every `.metal` file individually; it never stops at first error.
- The target is **0 failed shaders**. Any non-zero count is a blocker.
- `build_metal.dart` stops at the first error — do not use it for discovery.

## Fixing generator bugs

Fixes go in the Dart generator layer, never in the generated `.metal` files directly:

| Bug category | File to fix |
|---|---|
| Missing uniform in struct | `metal_fragment_builder.dart` → `_macroUniformTypes` or `_ensureModelViewProjForHPosition` |
| Untranslated HLSL function | `expression_translator.dart` → add a `LineTransformer` |
| Wrong type emitted | `metal_fragment_builder.dart` → `translateType` / `_outputType` |
| Shader IR not parsed correctly | `shader_ir_parser.dart` |
| Unpaired fragment shader | `tools/shader_port/config/shader_pair_overrides.json` → add explicit entry |

After any fix: re-run `dart tools/shader_port/bin/validate_migration.dart .` to confirm all stages pass.

## Every generator fix needs a regression test

```dart
// ✅ GOOD — fix + test
// test/metal_generator_test.dart or test/compile_check_test.dart
test('ModelViewProj is injected via HPosition fallback path', () {
  final String metal = buildMetal(data);
  expect(metal, contains('ModelViewProj'));
});
```

Tests live in `tools/shader_port/test/` and must not require the Metal compiler.

## Synthetic uniforms

If the generator body writes `uniforms.X` but `X` is not declared in the IR's `MainInput`, add it to `MetalFragmentBuilder._macroUniformTypes`. The `_computeSyntheticUniforms` method injects it only when `_translator.usesIdentifier('X')` is true.

For uniforms needed by fallback code (written after the translator runs), add a dedicated `_ensureXxx()` method called at the end of `_computeSyntheticUniforms`.

## Automated hook

A Cursor `stop` hook at `tools/shader_port/bin/hook_validate_migration.dart` runs automatically after every agent session that modifies shader-port files. If validation fails the hook re-engages the agent with the failure output (up to 3 retries via `loop_limit`).
